{
  "working_base": "49dca23e92a00a3f8a731ab7237b1556e305eef4",
  "scope": "Exploratory 0PN. Held radius 1; delayed flare; intake 0.25, with zero or half the independently defined trial flat reference drive. Carrier-following wall tracer with spherical angular symmetry; the archive cannot identify individual contacts, force-free slip, breakup or synchronized ordered-end work.",
  "contact_trial": "Two fixed signed transverse offsets, parallel stiffnesses from the same chi law at fixed axial sampling span. Normalized line work per initial elastic energy; starting at local order 0.95 with balanced net force and opposed internal strains. The matched outgoing uniform shear line is an assumed direct connection to ordered material, not a measured path into the feeding slab. Carrier, order, and geometry are prescribed in the weak shear limit. No active change of elementary rest lengths is imposed.",
  "work_units": "Energy per area in units of k0 times squared mismatch amplitude. Power into the line is F times ordered-end velocity in the held frame. Positive loss column is elastic energy removed by declining stiffness; its destination is unresolved. Last order 1e-6 is not a measured rupture. The energy left is an upper bound for later output only for continued monotone softening and no incoming waves or new work.",
  "controls": "Two carrier meshes, two conversion drives, equal softening, no mismatch, reversed mismatch, and receiver impedances 0.5/1/2. Span and entry prestrain require independent microscopic measurement; impedance can be fixed with independent shear traction and velocity in the ordered material.",
